  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_cardbert.npy",
    "space_digest": "1c7fb3995420711c",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 79,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "city-0 holds 26 of 79 cards and 8 verified members: CardBERT has pulled the goblin bodies and the storm spells (Empty the Warrens, Grapeshot, Haze of Rage) into one tribe-shaped mass, so the city reads as the deck's whole storm plan rather than one role.",
      "city-0-hood-0: Seething Song is the odd member of a goblin-lord neighbourhood (a ritual among creatures); likely a theme-space artefact, and it arguably belongs with city-2-hood-1's rituals.",
      "city-0-hood-2: Vandalblast and Daring Discovery are outliers in the burst-turn neighbourhood; Vandalblast is artifact removal and sits there by spell-shape, not by job.",
      "city-0-hood-1: Ancestors' Aid is an instant among creatures; it joins on Treasure/mana output, which is what the name follows.",
      "city-4 (verified 4) is the engine on the record: Zada plus the cantrip payloads of stacks 001 and 003. Renegade Tactics is in the payload hood but appears in no passing stack.",
      "city-4-hood-0 groups Zada with Krenko, Kreat, Pashalik Mons and Moggcatcher - legendary goblins clustered by being legends, not one job; Moggcatcher is a tutor, not a token engine.",
      "city-2-hood-0 is mixed: Blasphemous Act, Chaos Warp and Goblin Negotiation are answers, Faithless Looting and Past in Flames are graveyard flashback; the split reads arbitrary and the name says both halves.",
      "city-3-hood-0 contains two lands (Fountainport, War Room) alongside Sol Ring and Throne of Eldraine - lands that draw clustered with artifacts that draw, so the mana-base city (city-5) is not every land.",
      "city-3-hood-1: Swiftfoot Boots protects rather than multiplies; the other three (Ruby Medallion, Roaming Throne, Skullclamp) scale what the goblins already do."
    ]
  },
